/* ============================================================
   TEST PAGE 4 — THE PERFUMERS' GRAPH (2026-11-06, in place of "The Scent
   Landscape").

   The owner: "replace tp4 with another iteration of the perfumers page,
   and this one should be something like images 5 and 6. It should have a
   table where you can select the perfumers and then it would take you to a
   node, which would have subnodes of houses, then further subnodes of
   perfumes." And then, seeing the first of it: "that looks ugly, try to
   make it as close to the reference i have given you earlier as possible,
   not just a few lines." Image 5: a network of thousands of dark specks on
   a pale grey, joined in hairlines, gathered in dense clouds and strung
   between them, in three dimensions, framed by the corners of a camera —
   OBJECT and its name at the top, the word looked at spelled down the left
   with where each letter stands, STAGE 5: LETTERS at the foot, TOTAL at the
   bottom right, a broken ring at the bottom left. Image 6: a graph view — a
   round field of thousands of nodes and fine lines, the busiest with fans.

   Here every node is the ledger's, as image 5's are its book's: every
   PERFUMER, every one of its HOUSES, every PERFUME, every LETTER of every
   perfume's name (as the book's words are its letters), and every NOTE the
   Note Library files for the perfumes on the site — a perfume joined to its
   notes, so the notes the clouds share string them together. About three
   thousand specks, turning slowly in three dimensions; the busiest clouds
   (Prin Lomros', Nicholas Nilsson's) the darkest.
   THE TABLE on the right lists the perfumers (sortable, searchable); a row
   pressed takes the camera to its cloud and its houses are named; a house
   pressed, its perfumes; a perfume pressed, its letters, named on the
   field and spelled down the left, letter by letter, as image 5's word is,
   and its notes lit across the field. The stages say how deep you are:
   1 PERFUMERS, 2 HOUSES, 3 PERFUMES, 4 LETTERS. A drag turns it, the wheel
   and the keys come closer; the ground is image 5's grey or image 6's dark.

   HOW IT IS DRAWN: laid out once, in three dimensions, cloud by cloud;
   every frame each speck is turned and put in perspective, the lines drawn
   in three strokes and the specks in three fills, by how near they are.

   A snapshot of the site's Perfumers ledger and of the notes the Note
   Library files for its perfumes, written in above: nothing on the site
   reads this page, and it reads nothing of the site.
   ============================================================ */
